        "root_concepts": "[analytic, number]",
        "section": "number-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Analytic Number Theory",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Examples:\n  Σ 1·n^{-s} = ζ(s)\n  Σ φ(n)n^{-s} = ζ(s-1)/ζ(s)\n  Σ μ(n)n^{-s} = 1/ζ(s)         [Möbius function is \"inverse\" of 1]\n  Σ Λ(n)n^{-s} = -ζ'(s)/ζ(s)   [von Mangoldt function]\n  Σ d(n)n^{-s} = ζ(s)²          [d(n) = # divisors]\n  Σ σ_k(n)n^{-s} = ζ(s)ζ(s-k)  [σ_k = sum of k-th powers of divisors]"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-ANALYTIC-NUMBER-THEORY.md#009",
